^SAMPLE = GSM2782576
!Sample_title = TEX_No_virus_1
!Sample_geo_accession = GSM2782576
!Sample_status = Public on Sep 01 2020
!Sample_submission_date = Sep 13 2017
!Sample_last_update_date = Sep 01 2020
!Sample_type = SRA
!Sample_channel_count = 1
!Sample_source_name_ch1 = TEX cell line
!Sample_organism_ch1 = Homo sapiens
!Sample_taxid_ch1 = 9606
!Sample_characteristics_ch1 = cell type: Engineered leukemic stem cell line
!Sample_characteristics_ch1 = tissue: Blood
!Sample_characteristics_ch1 = genetic modification: Wild-type
!Sample_treatment_protocol_ch1 = shRNA knockdown was performed with lentiviral infections. 2 mL of virus was added to 5 mL of media containing 5.0 x 106 cells and protamine sulfate (5 µg/mL) followed by overnight incubation (37C, 5% CO2). The following day, cells were centrifuged and washed, and re-suspended in 25 mL fresh medium with appropriate puromycin concentration (2.0 ug/ml) and subjected to selection for 3 days.
!Sample_growth_protocol_ch1 = TEX leukemic cells were cultured in IMDM with 20% FCS, 100  units/mL streptomycin, 100 µg/mL penicillin, 20 ng/mL stem cell factor (SCF), 2 ng/mL  IL-3, and 2 mM L-glutamine.
!Sample_molecule_ch1 = total RNA
!Sample_extract_protocol_ch1 = RNeasy Plus Mini Kit. Quality of total RNA samples were checked on an Agilent Bioanalyzer 2100 RNA Nano chip following Agilent Technologies’ recommendation. Concentration was measured by Qubit RNA HS Assay ona Qubit fluorometer (ThermoFisher)
!Sample_extract_protocol_ch1 = RNA library preparation was performed following the NEB NEBNext Ultra Directional Library Preparation protocol
!Sample_data_processing = Reads adapters were removed using Trim Galore v. 0.4.0 and reads were aligned against hg19 using Tophat v. 2.0.11. Read counts per gene were obtained through htseq-count v.0.6.1p2 in the mode “intersection_nonempty”.
!Sample_data_processing = After removing genes whose cpm (counts per million reads) were less than 0.5, edgeR R package v.3.8.6 was used to normalize the data using the TMM (trimmed mean of M values) method and to estimate differential expression by applying a generalized linear model between the control TEX samples and the TEX cells isolated after MTCH2 knockdown.
!Sample_data_processing = Raw gene counts are loaded and sample-normalized using DESeq v.1.18.0
!Sample_data_processing = False Discovery Rate, calculated by Benjamini-Hochberg method (useful for hits selection)
!Sample_data_processing = Two-condition differential expression was done with the edgeR R package, v.3.8.6
!Sample_data_processing = Genome_build: hg19 (RefSeq gene models)
!Sample_data_processing = Supplementary_files_format_and_content: tab-delimited text files include RPKM values for each Sample
!Sample_platform_id = GPL16791
